<!-- SECTION 9: How the ratio changes the angle -->
<section id="arctan-ratio" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>How the Opposite-to-Adjacent Ratio Affects the Angle</h2>
  <p>The ratio <span set:html={rich('[[a/b]]')} /> determines angle <span set:html={rich('[[A]]')} />. A small ratio produces a small acute angle, equal sides produce exactly 45 degrees, and an opposite side longer than the adjacent side produces an angle greater than 45 degrees. A ratio greater than 1 is completely valid for tangent, which sets it apart from sine and cosine. Proportional triangles share the same angles, and scaling both legs by the same positive factor leaves the angle unchanged. As the ratio grows extremely large, the angle approaches 90 degrees without reaching it for finite positive side lengths.</p>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full border-collapse text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-outline-variant/30">
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-left font-semibold">Opposite a</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-left font-semibold">Adjacent b</th>
          <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-left font-semibold">Ratio a/b</th>
          <th class="py-2 text-left font-semibold">Angle A</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-outline-variant/20"><td class="py-2 pr-4">1</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">4</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">0.25</td><td class="py-2">Approximately 14.04&deg;</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-outline-variant/20"><td class="py-2 pr-4">1</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">2</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">0.5</td><td class="py-2">Approximately 26.57&deg;</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-outline-variant/20"><td class="py-2 pr-4">1</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">1</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">1</td><td class="py-2">45&deg;</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-outline-variant/20"><td class="py-2 pr-4">2</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">1</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">2</td><td class="py-2">Approximately 63.43&deg;</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">4</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">1</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">4</td><td class="py-2">Approximately 75.96&deg;</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The pattern is clear: the side ratio determines the shape of the triangle, not its overall size. Double both legs and the angle stays exactly the same.</p>

